  {"date": "2025-09-20", "venue": "Hampton Coliseum", "city": "Hampton", "state": "VA", "gap": 9, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "One of the more interesting (possibly?) Fish-driven jams. If interested in following a different sort of percussion rinse - a riveting (albeit subdued) amalgamation of our favorite drummer's different styles and sounds - you can do much worse. While his play belies the suggestion the improvisation is in any way aimless, what's more: A true sense, here, that Trey is creeping closer, if not to outright (lowercase) space, than certainly surrendering to the air - his tone at times incredibly surprising, masterfully matching his introspective ideas. Or: Rather different from the other versions.", "out": "->", "prev": "Simple", "in": ">", "next": "Gotta Jibboo", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2026-01-31", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 9, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "As if inspired by the massive reading of \"A Song I Heard the Ocean Sing\" that preceded it, this take spreads itself out at a luxuriating, gradual pace. Melodic and rhythmic elasticity mercurially envelop the music, as is custom for \"Sea of Stars\", particularly colored by Fishman's finesse-driven rhythmic flux as well as Trey's both clean and affected textural playing. Play then forms up behind a spaced-out minor key drive, sounding almost threateningly similar to \"ASIHTOS\", building up to smokey, hazy peak before > \"Meatstick\".", "out": ">", "prev": "A Song I Heard the Ocean Sing", "in": "->", "next": "Meatstick", "nb": 1},
